30,2,1,talk,Minato,,The earth-moving firms are worried about clay and slippage. We should be careful about big digs.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,1,talk,May,,It seems the cost to maintain planted areas is triple that of hard surfaces. That's a scary gap.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"The old overflow basin is still perfect, but the paved apron is a mess. Nature seems to last longer here.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,1,talk,Victoria,,"Our staff is tiny now, but we have volunteers for habitat and sports. We can't do everything ourselves.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"People just want to get to the tram stop on firm ground, and the drainage is failing.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,2,talk,Minato,,"@Shunichi, does that mean we need more paving or better drains?","{""words"":11,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,2,talk,May,,"@Victoria, if we have few staff, we can't afford high-maintenance greenery.","{""words"":11,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@May, but the paving I saw was patched three times already. Maybe hard surfaces aren't the answer.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Shizue, that's true, but we have no one to water trees. The staff roll has plummeted.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Minato, we need something that handles water and doesn't block the tram commuters.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,3,talk,Minato,,I'm worried about the center of the park. The depot says we can't hoard it without closing the gate.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,3,talk,May,,"If the upkeep for plants is that high, we need a plan that is simple or funded.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,3,talk,Shizue,,I remember the eastern avenue trees died because of no watering. We must be realistic.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,3,talk,Victoria,,The volunteers are a key resource. They already do habitat and sports work.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,The heat is rising and the culverts are capped. We need a solution for the water.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
